// A designated file beneath an organisational folder, which is refused rather
// than drawing a module two levels down.
//
// org/ holds no file named org.cone, so it is organisational and its files are
// the enclosing module's. deep/ inside it holds deep.cone, which is the shape of
// a module folder -- but a module folder must be a DIRECT child of its parent
// module's folder, so that the module tree's shape mirrors the folder tree's. A
// module here would have a parent whose folder is not its folder's parent, which
// the tree has no shape for. The diagnostic naming this file is in cases.toml.
//
// What happens after the refusal is the second diagnostic: the folder stays
// organisational, so this file is swept into the enclosing module like any other
// file of org/, and a swept file has no module to declare.

mod deep;          //~ ErrorModDcl "first statement" follow-on

fn deepFn(n i64) i64 {
  2i64;
}
